 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-17",
  "asof": "2026-09-19 17:21 UTC",
  "headline": "The Nasdaq cleared two sigma for the first time in a week \u2014 because the bond market decided the hike bought credibility",
  "standfirst": "The session after the decision did what the decision did not. The Nasdaq rose 1.67%, a two-sigma move and the first thing on this board to travel outside its ordinary range in a week; the S&P added 1.14%, the Russell 1.09% and the Dow 0.71% \u2014 Wednesday\u2019s split run exactly backwards. The ten-year fell 5bp to 4.94%, back under the five-percent line, and the VIX collapsed 12.14% to 15.56. A curve that rallies after a hawkish hike and an upgraded dot plot is a bond market saying the Fed bought credibility with this move. Every position in the book closed green and none came near a stop; crude fell a third straight session to about $101.25. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R for a fourth session. Today the Bank of Japan decides and roughly $6.2 trillion of US options exposure expires in the same session.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "BoJ and $6.2tn of expiry, today, same session",
    "title": "Two events, one session, and a book carrying full risk into both",
    "items": [
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "BOJ",
      "html": "<b>Bank of Japan decision</b> \u2014 25bp to 1.25%, a 31-year high, all but fully priced",
      "when": "today \u00b7 2026-09-18",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-opex",
      "tag": "OPEX",
      "html": "<b>Triple witching</b> \u2014 about $6.2tn of US options exposure expiring",
      "when": "today \u00b7 2026-09-18",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "OKTA",
      "html": "<b>Oktane</b> \u2014 investor summit webcast",
      "when": "Wed \u00b7 2026-09-23",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-fomc",
      "tag": "FOMC",
      "html": "<b>Next Fed decision</b> \u2014 the dot plot implies one more hike in 2026",
      "when": "Oct \u00b7 2026-10-28",
      "kind": "calendar"
     }
    ],
    "note": "<b>The size is the point.</b> Citadel Securities put roughly <b>$6.2 trillion</b> of US options exposure expiring today \u2014 about 23% of all outstanding exposure, and possibly more by settlement. It does not clear in one moment: standard index options settle on the opening quotation, PM-settled contracts in the afternoon, single stocks separately. So the pressure is spread across the session rather than concentrated at the bell, and the direction is set by where the index sits relative to heavily populated strikes rather than by any view."
   }
  ],
  "ondeck": "<b>The size is the point.</b> Citadel Securities put roughly <b>$6.2 trillion</b> of US options exposure expiring today \u2014 about 23% of all outstanding exposure, and possibly more by settlement. It does not clear in one moment: standard index options settle on the opening quotation, PM-settled contracts in the afternoon, single stocks separately. So the pressure is spread across the session rather than concentrated at the bell, and the direction is set by where the index sits relative to heavily populated strikes rather than by any view.",
